From ac459dc24d1398943f1f934d0312e3aa4e89273a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:02:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] kv-cache fp8: Flash Next e4m3 attention caches

--kv-cache fp8 (one rank, our glue; not with --slide, a captured set, the KV
pages or --learn-conversations) keeps each position's keys and values as e4m3
codes with a power-of-two scale a (position, KV head) row; 1,056 bytes a
position and layer instead of 2,048. The KV8 device code is split into
flashnext_kv8.cuh and its launch records register; the lean and changelog
gates read clean. Carries the 0005 reader half (stage_kv8/kv8_widen8).

Squash of stack commits ec2526436..a1f525319 (port-0003-kv8 @ 7ff8292bc).
