 - `--parallel N` admits N streams. Each stream's caches are its own: about 110 MiB of DeltaNet state and the n-gram
   tail, plus 28 KiB a token of keys, values and indexer keys, and with drafts its MTP head's cache.
+- `--kv-cache fp8` (one rank, the engine's own glue; not with `--slide`, a captured set, the KV pages or
+  `--learn-conversations`) keeps keys and values as e4m3 codes with a power-of-two scale a position and KV head: 1,056 bytes
+  a position and layer instead of 2,048, so a token's caches take about 17.5 KiB instead of 30 KiB (12 layers and the MTP
+  head's). The indexer's keys, the pooled blocks and the DeltaNet states stay bf16. Attention reads the codes widened to
+  bf16 exactly, so it is the bf16 kernels' arithmetic on rows rounded to e4m3: lossy against a bf16 cache, deterministic
+  for a given prompt. bf16 stays the default.
 - `--no-drafts` serves without the MTP head; `"draft": false` on a request does the same for that request.
 - `TF_FLASHNEXT_READOUT_ROWS` (default 64, `0` never) is the rows from which the hyper-connection read-out takes the prompt
   tiles. Same bits either way; `128` keeps 16-stream decode rounds on the row kernels, up to 7% quicker on a GB10.
